  "exec_summary": "The Anti-Money Laundering Authority (AMLA) has published draft guidelines on ongoing monitoring under Article 26(5) of the Anti-Money Laundering Regulation (AMLR), a significant EU regulatory development. In Belgium, there are no notable developments this week, but the AMLA guidelines will be relevant to Belgian financial institutions. The European Insurance and Occupational Pensions Authority (EIOPA) has also called for industry opinion on the supervision of reinsurance undertakings, which may impact Belgian insurers. The AMLA guidelines are a key development for the EU financial sector, and institutions should review them to ensure compliance with the AMLR.",
